{
  "name": "Track Amazon prices for your keywords with Scrapewise and log them in Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -960,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 440,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## Daily Amazon price tracker\n\nFor every keyword you list, Scrapewise returns what Amazon sells: title, ASIN, price, rating, review count, image and link. One dated row per product, so the sheet becomes a price history.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a Scrapewise API key with full access at portal.scrapewise.ai.\n2. In **Search Amazon**, add a *Bearer Auth* credential and paste the key as the token.\n3. In **Save prices to Google Sheets**, pick your Google account and set the spreadsheet and tab.\n4. Put your keywords and marketplace in **Keywords and marketplace**.\n\n**Cost:** 1 credit per result page. One keyword and one page answer straight away. Two or more keywords run as a background job \u2014 this workflow then picks the rows up with **Get job results**.\n\n**One answer carries one page of rows.** If **Get job results** comes back with `truncated: true` and a `nextPage`, there are more rows waiting. This template saves the first page, which is plenty for a handful of keywords. For a long list, send that `nextPage` value back into **Get job results** as `page` and keep going until `truncated` is false.\n\n**Marketplaces:** com, co.uk, de, fr, it, es, ca, com.au, co.jp, in, com.br, com.mx, nl, sg, ae, sa, pl, se, com.tr, eg, com.be"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Every morning at 7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
